---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const facts = [
  ['What', 'AI engineering consultancy'],
  ['Where', 'Sheffield, UK — remote engagements'],
  ['Who', 'Damian — senior software engineer, many years in the industry'],
  ['Security', 'CosmWasm / Go audit work, paid bounty findings'],
  ['Stack', 'Claude Code · Python · Go · TypeScript · cloud AI services'],
];
---

<Base
  title="About — Closed Loop"
  description="Closed Loop is an AI engineering consultancy in Sheffield, UK, run by a senior software engineer with many years in the industry. Agentic systems, Claude Code, and end-to-end system building."
>
  <section class="container top">
    <div class="intro">
      <p class="eyebrow" data-reveal>About</p>
      <h1 data-reveal style="--i:1">What Closed Loop is.</h1>
      <p class="lede" data-reveal style="--i:2">
        Closed Loop is an AI engineering consultancy. It designs, builds and hands
        over production AI systems — autonomous development loops, multi-agent
        pipelines, and the infrastructure underneath them — for businesses that
        need the output to be verified, not just impressive.
      </p>
    </div>
    <dl class="facts" data-reveal="left" style="--i:2">
      {facts.map(([k, v]) => (
        <div><dt>{k}</dt><dd>{v}</dd></div>
      ))}
    </dl>
  </section>

  <article class="prose-shell prose body">
    <p data-reveal>
      The name is the method. An open loop is a prompt in and text out with nobody
      checking. A closed loop feeds its own output back through a gate — verified,
      reviewed, recorded — before it is allowed to count. Every system Closed Loop
      ships is built that way, and every rule in it came from a failure that was
      documented rather than hidden.
    </p>
    <h2 data-reveal>How the work is done</h2>
    <p data-reveal>
      State in plain files, so anyone — human or agent — can read the truth.
      Verification by evidence rather than assertion. Separation of duties enforced
      by capability, not by prompts. The articles on this site are those methods
      written up from the inside: the architecture, the gates, and the scars.
    </p>
    <h2 data-reveal>The engineer behind it</h2>
    <p data-reveal>
      Closed Loop is run by Damian, a senior software engineer in Sheffield with
      many years of experience shipping production software in demanding, regulated
      industries. Alongside client work he builds and runs his own AI systems:
      autonomous development loops on Claude Code, multi-agent audit pipelines for
      Web3 security work, and a personal-assistant harness that manages a real
      life — calendars, finances, health, memory — through plain files and
      scheduled agents.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li data-reveal style="--i:0"><strong>AI engineering</strong> — agentic loops, multi-agent orchestration, Claude Code skills/subagents, RAG pipelines, evaluation.</li>
      <li data-reveal style="--i:1"><strong>Production delivery</strong> — many years delivering full products on short cycles; remote contracts across regulated industries and fintech.</li>
      <li data-reveal style="--i:2"><strong>Web3 security</strong> — CosmWasm/Golang audit work with a custom multi-agent auditing system; paid bounty findings.</li>
      <li data-reveal style="--i:3"><strong>Systems from scratch</strong> — once designed and built an award-winning five-barrel microbrewery from raw materials, control electronics included. Whole-system thinking is the throughline.</li>
    </ul>
    <p data-reveal>
      Want to work together? See <a href="/services/">services</a>, or email
      <a href="mailto:hello@closed-loop.dev">hello@closed-loop.dev</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
<style>
  .top {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.3fr) minmax(0, 0.9fr);
    gap: 3rem;
    align-items: end;
    padding-block: clamp(3rem, 8vh, 5.5rem) 2rem;
  }
  .top h1 { font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 5.5vw, 4rem); margin-block: 1rem 1.25rem; }
  .lede { font-size: 1.15rem; margin: 0; max-width: 40rem; }
  .facts {
    margin: 0;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 10px;
    background: var(--surface);
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .facts div {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 6rem 1fr;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding: 0.85rem 1.25rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }
  .facts div:first-child { border-top: 0; }
  .facts dt { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.72rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.12em; color: var(--accent); padding-top: 0.25rem; }
  .facts dd { margin: 0; font-family: var(--font-heading); color: var(--text-strong); }
  .body { padding-block: 1rem 2rem; }
  .body h2 { margin-block: 2rem 0.6rem; }
  @media (max-width: 860px) { .top { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>
